    {"dot":"cyan","title":"B06a scope (model/provider/routing)","items":["Part of B06-ai-platform split (108 routes/18 controllers reconciled). Modules: ai-model (26/5), model-residency (14/1), ai-provider-connection (8/1), ai-routing-policy (11/1), ai-service-admin (9/1) = 68 routes / 9 controllers.","AI model registry: admin/catalogue/registration/discovery/jobs under /admin/ai-models. Residency: /admin/model-residency. Provider connections: /admin/providers. Routing policies: /admin/routing-policies. AI service admin: /admin/ai-services.","Grouped endpoint nodes for readability; route-level contracts/examples summarized in cards."]},
    {"dot":"violet","title":"Example input/output (representative)","items":["Model registration/discovery/jobs: admin requests register/discover/download/unregister models or manage model jobs -> model registry records/job metadata. Verify artifact URLs, credentials, and async job behavior.","Model residency: policy/state CRUD requests -> residency policy/state responses (data residency constraints for model usage).","Provider connection/routing policy: create/update provider credentials/endpoints and routing rules -> resolved provider/routing config. Verify secret storage/authref handling and policy precedence.","AI service admin: service configuration requests -> AI service config records. Exact DTOs and downstream service wiring should be verified."]},
    {"dot":"emerald","title":"Evidence and limitations","items":["Repo https://github.com/ArcaAI/project-hope.git @ 8cb2e5e8e6bbddf5ee7c676782ebb5ad683c23a0. Controller/service sources verified in local tree (ai-model services, residency, provider connection, routing policy).","Downstreams: AI platform config data store (Postgres/Prisma) and external AI providers/model artifacts/inference targets (config-driven).","Limitations: grouped endpoint nodes (68 routes/9 controllers); AiServiceAdmin service implementation path not separately verified; secret/authref/model artifact handling and routing precedence are implementation-specific — reconcile with OpenAPI/implementation."]}
